.env
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.csv
# ...but NOT the committed research provenance artifacts. The blanket *.csv above
# silently ate four fixtures that tools/overnight_gap_risk_study.py declares
# SHA-256 hashes for (entry_bar_5m_ordering_2026.csv, entry_bar_1m_resolution_2026.csv,
# tqqq_corporate_actions_2010_2026.csv, qqq_distributions_2010_2026.csv). Their JSON
# sibling in the same directory and the same commit survived, because only the .csv
# extension matched — `git add` on an ignored path is a silent no-op. Those four
# fixtures are the sole evidence behind ~32% of RESEARCH_WEB.md and cannot be
# regenerated offline. Committing them is the one action that restores it.
!docs/research/data/*.csv
.DS_Store
venv/
*.egg-info/
experiments.jsonl
sweep_results_*.json
live/state.db
state.db
local_ops/
local_logs/
.ibkr-paper.env
*.ibkr-paper.env

# Raw databases — never commit; export sanitized JSON instead
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
# Runtime / operational artifacts
*.pid
*.tmp
data/live_runs/tmp_*/
local_backups/
local_runtime/
# Strategy-funnel offline research output (survivor/rejection cards)
data/funnel_runs/
# Graphify ingestion output + the bridge's suggestions (never auto-committed)
graphify-out/
data/graphify_suggestions/

# Coverage artifacts (CI/dev only — see .github/workflows/test.yml)
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
htmlcov/
.pytest_cache/
